---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import LoopFigure from '../components/LoopFigure.astro';
import CampaignFigure from '../components/CampaignFigure.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { delta, deltaCta, deltaNav, site } from '../config';

// Delta's page: the cockpit where intent enters the run, and an example campaign.
---

<Base
  title={`${delta.name}: ${delta.title}`}
  description={delta.description}
  nav={deltaNav}
  cta={deltaCta}
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="Delta"
    title={delta.tagline}
    lede="An autonomous system does not run on a single command. A person states intent while the work is moving, and the run changes. Delta is the surface where that intent enters the loop."
    body="The machine is the sum of the intents that enter the loop."
  />

  <Section
    id="loop"
    label="The loop"
    title="A run is not a command"
    lede="A command asks for an output and waits. An autonomous system keeps running, and a person can enter at any point with a new intent, a limit, or a correction. The result is the sum of those entries."
  >
    <LoopFigure />
    <p class="note">
      The cockpit is where the operator reads the run and enters the next intent.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="cockpit"
    label="Cockpit"
    title="What the operator sees and changes"
    lede="Delta shows the state of the run and gives the operator a way into it."
  >
    <dl class="spec">
      <dt>What the operator can change</dt>
      <dd>A new intent, a new limit, or a stop, entered while the work is moving.</dd>
      <dt>What is running</dt>
      <dd>The project and the work in flight, with the state the record gives them.</dd>
      <dt>Who claimed it</dt>
      <dd>The claim, the operator, and the authority that took the work.</dd>
      <dt>What bounded it</dt>
      <dd>The hints and the terms that limited the run.</dd>
    </dl>

    <p class="note">
      Scrub the run backwards and the state follows the record. The operator can enter the next
      intent from any point.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="example"
    label="Example"
    title="The villa evacuation, an example campaign"
    lede="An emergency lift on the Monaco coast shows the loop in a run. The operator's intent and the hospital's bound enter while the work is moving. The run starts when the emergency is declared and ends when treatment starts."
  >
    <CampaignFigure />

    <ul class="metrics">
      <li class="metric">
        <span class="metric__value">1,164</span>
        <span class="metric__label">records in the run</span>
      </li>
      <li class="metric">
        <span class="metric__value">5</span>
        <span class="metric__label">objectives, one with a deadline</span>
      </li>
      <li class="metric">
        <span class="metric__value">75 s</span>
        <span class="metric__label">the scan has to reach the hospital</span>
      </li>
      <li class="metric">
        <span class="metric__value">3</span>
        <span class="metric__label">checks in the scenario</span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="note">
      The scan is written at 80 seconds, three seconds inside its window. The campaign line shows
      five of five met, and the record behind each one.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="contact"
    label="Contact"
    title="Bring a run to the cockpit."
    lede="We are choosing the first design partners. If you run a situation that has to be replayed and understood, write to us."
    band
  >
    <p><a class="btn btn--accent" href={`mailto:${site.contact}`}>Write to us</a></p>
  </Section>
</Base>
